# CI/CD Setup Guide

This project uses **GitHub Actions** for continuous integration and deployment.

---

## Workflows

| File | Trigger | What it does |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `ci.yml` | Every push / PR to `main` or `develop` | Lint → Test → Build on Node 18 & 20 |
| `cd.yml` | Push to `main` only | Deploys backend to Railway, frontend to Vercel |
| `security.yml` | Every Monday 09:00 UTC | `npm audit` both packages |

---

## Required GitHub Secrets

Go to **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret** and add:

### Always required
| Secret | Where to get it |
|--------|----------------|
| `OPENWEATHER_API_KEY` | [openweathermap.org/api](https://openweathermap.org/api) (free tier) |

### For Vercel (frontend deploy)
| Secret | Where to get it |
|--------|----------------|
| `VERCEL_TOKEN` | vercel.com → Account Settings → Tokens |
| `VERCEL_ORG_ID` | `vercel.json` or Vercel dashboard → Project Settings |
| `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID` | Vercel dashboard → Project Settings |
| `REACT_APP_API_URL` | Your deployed Railway backend URL, e.g. `https://weather-api.up.railway.app/api` |

### For Railway (backend deploy)
| Secret | Where to get it |
|--------|----------------|
| `RAILWAY_TOKEN` | railway.app → Account Settings → Tokens |

### Optional
| Secret | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` | Slack deploy-failure notifications |

